#{[17592186564520 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564520 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158568" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564520 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564520 #edb/ref 1071 "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined as \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(y+1).\n$$\n\nEvaluate this function at the point $(-3,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564520 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "be7cd3c6-b4d8-58fc-a0bb-f9185ad55778" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564520 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(-3,1),$ we substitute $x=-3$ and $y=1$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3,1) & =x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(y+1)\\,{|}_{(-3,1)} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(1+1) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{arccos}⁡2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564533 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564533 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158185" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564533 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564533 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-y)}{{e}^{x}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564533 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e5fbae1b-fa0a-5638-bec4-5b64d04c9a07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564533 #edb/ref 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nNotice that ${e}^{x}>0$ for all $x.$ Therefore, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y>0\\,⟹\\,x>y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x>y\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564534 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564534 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158191" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564534 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564534 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-{x}^{2})}{y}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564534 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e70a4727-f486-57b6-aa40-dbf0dba8fb16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564534 #edb/ref 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}1-{x}^{2}>0 \\\\ y\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-1<x<1 \\\\ y\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1<x<1,\\,y\\ne 0\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564538 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564538 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158196" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564538 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564538 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $g(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564538 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f90f5dc8-4e9d-5e87-800a-708d8b32cd8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564538 #edb/ref 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1\\ge 0\n$$\n\nSince the inequality ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1\\ge 0$ is true for all values of $x$ and $y,$ the domain of the function $f$ is the entire $xy$-plane.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/40/402d90507403eabf4cd35cde83a45c9fa2d8080347e1debb0e2463be408b489b.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
